content.text:
Now add `.duel-versus-card` --versus-glow maybe JS only sets color not glow. Could set `--versus-glow` from crystal with alpha; JS set only color. We can set in reveal:
```
card.style.setProperty('--versus-glow', `rgba(${hexToRgb(color)},.14)`);
```
hexToRgb exists. We'll add later.

Now disassembly shift. Modify layout and labels.

Current:
```
const centerY = .08;
disassemblyCamera.position.set(0, centerY + .04, distance);
disassemblyCamera.lookAt(0, centerY, 0);
```
Change to `frameOffsetX`:
```
const frameOffsetX = width < 760 ? .18 : .42;
disassemblyCamera.position.set(frameOffsetX, centerY+.04, distance);
lookAt(frameOffsetX, centerY, 0);
```
Need be sure camera projection centers lookAt point; object at x=0 appears left. Good.

Labels centerX add:
```
const labelBias = width < 760 ? 10 : 20;
const centerX = width / 2 + labelBias;
```
But `left = Math.max(sx + 74, centerX + 108)`; at narrow all side right, text begins to right of saber; if saber shifted left, plus bias. Nice.
Maybe shift by more: user says "move light saber display a bit to left and text just a tiny bit right". Camera .45 world ~ maybe 5%, labels 20px. Good.

But if "overlap" persists on right labels, increase camera .55. Let's test after.

Also top-left readout can overlap shifted labels? Labels vertically centered; readout at top. ok.

Patch.

